  "summary": "Six preprints from mid-November 2026 pair rational molecular glue design with computational binder design and mutational mapping of drug-sensitive targets.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is rational engineering of protein-protein interfaces and ligand sensitivity. Two preprints address molecular glue degraders: TrIP-MGRD targets transient PPI pockets, supported by a CDK12-DDB1 cryo-EM structure and glue C432, while a HER2-directed antibody conjugate delivers a cyclin K glue degrader with HER2-selective CCNK degradation. Others apply computation to binder design: a shared latent space for affinity-guided PDZ-binding peptides, including off-target-aware and dual-target design, and MobGen for de novo monobodies against the SARS-CoV-2 RBD. Complementary mapping studies cover nanobody bias toward the BasC intracellular cavity and paired deep mutational scanning of Lck producing a nilotinib-sensitized variant. The new element is moving from empirical discovery toward designed, selective, interface-aware modulation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
}
